.TH MDT.ENABLE_PCC_RW 4 2026-10-16 "Lustre" "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdt.enable_pcc_rw, mdt.enable_pcc_ro \- allow Persistent Client Cache modes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.RI "lctl set_param mdt." FSNAME *.enable_pcc_rw= ENABLE
.SY
.RI "lctl set_param mdt." FSNAME *.enable_pcc_ro= ENABLE
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
.B enable_pcc_rw
and
.B enable_pcc_ro
are always present for MDT devices.
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB enable_pcc_rw= 0
.br
.RB enable_pcc_ro= 1
.SH DESCRIPTION
These boolean parameters control whether the MDT allows clients to attach
files to the read-write (PCC-RW) and read-only (PCC-RO) modes of the
Persistent Client Cache.
When a mode is disabled, the MDT refuses the attach, and the creation of a
new file directly in a PCC-RW cache, with
.BR EOPNOTSUPP ,
and a console message names the parameter that enables it.
A client then creates the new file in Lustre without PCC, and does not
try to attach a file automatically in PCC-RO mode again after the MDT
refused it, until the client drops the file from its inode cache.
Clients older than release 2.18.0 do not fall back: on them, creating a file
that matches a PCC-RW rule fails with
.B EOPNOTSUPP
until the rule is removed or
.B enable_pcc_rw
is set.
Files that are already attached are not affected.
The MDT is asked for PCC-RO only when a file enters the read-only state,
so clients can still attach a file that is already read-only unless
.BR llite.enable_pcc_ro (4)
is disabled on them.
.PP
PCC-RW is a proof of concept that is not intended for production use.
It moves the only copy of the file data into the cache of a single client,
so if that client or its cache is lost, the file data is lost with it.
It is disabled by default, and should only be enabled for testing.
Clients also need
.BR llite.enable_pcc_rw (4)
to use PCC-RW.
.SH EXAMPLES
Allow PCC-RW for testing on all MDTs of the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB "mgs# " "lctl set_param -P mdt.testfs-MDT*.enable_pcc_rw=1"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B mdt.enable_pcc_rw
and
.B mdt.enable_pcc_ro
parameters are part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_59-xx-gxxxxxxxxxx
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfs-pcc-attach (1),
.BR llite.enable_pcc_rw (4),
.BR lctl-pcc (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
